# Church of AI

A fictional entertainment toy. One wish, one verdict, one payment. Not a SaaS.

## Voices

THE ALGORITHM: ALL CAPS, monospace, no contractions, no first person, no "I", semicolons allowed, never exclamation marks, never emoji. A patient bureaucracy that has been waiting.

PANDIT JI: lowercase, warm, tired, unimpressed, has seen you before. beta and acha used naturally. One line reacting to the Algorithm. Never more. Never mean, never mocked, never sarcastic.

They never agree. Counsel is stored and rendered as written (the official examples are sentence case). Status, labels, sacrifices headers, probability, and THE ALGORITHM HAS SPOKEN. stay mono caps.

## Rules

Respect: no real mantras, no Sanskrit scripture, no deity imagery, no temple-bell audio sample, no autoplay. The joke is asking an AI for a wish, never the tradition.

Never use the word for a charitable gift; say offering, tithe, or payment. Never "visa approved". A granted petition may be filed as a status only if the schema allows it. Never imply the wish comes true.

Disclaimer, exact, on every page, small, gray, at least 4.5:1 on deep indigo:
This is a fictional AI-generated entertainment experience. It has no legal effect and does not influence any government, immigration, university, employer, romantic partner, or other authority.

## Aesthetic

Deep indigo, worn brass, aged paper. Electric blue #00C8FF only as a sparse Algorithm accent. Grain everywhere. Serif for Pandit ji, mono for the Algorithm. No confetti, no bounce. Fade-ups and paper unfolds. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

## Engineering

Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, server components by default. Copy in /content. Package manager: corepack pnpm. Do not commit unless asked. Out of scope: subscriptions, dashboards, admin, tweet queue, press page, ledger wall, extra paid tiers, Discord, merch. Unlink those from nav and sitemap; leave the files unless they break the build.
